# Rust profile schema and CLI roundtrip

## Scope and existing evidence

Create canonical Rust-only load, inspect, validate, and save commands for one
notebook and one handwriting profile. No Python is involved.

The historical theoretical design remains separate from executable scope.
This record is complete only for the native Rust CLI round-trip checked
on November 3, 2026.

## Acceptance decision

Completed — practical native CLI acceptance on November 3, 2026.

The `atrament-profiles notebook` and `handwriting` modes perform native Rust
file creation, canonical load/inspect, editing and save to explicit paths.
An executable smoke check created a boxed-date notebook, reopened the file
byte-for-byte, and saved a modified copy without changing its source.
The same check created a handwriting statistics file with an exact NFD
diacritic override, reopened identical JSON, and saved an edited-seed
copy while preserving its source.

For both profile types, opening malformed JSON with explicit `--replace`
refused before changing the selected existing output sentinel file.
The Rust harness also exercises invalid statistics, source preservation,
file type refusal and symlink protection in
`tests/backend/profile-editor-cli/composition/lib.rs`.
The 23 focused CLI tests, strict CLI Clippy, and
`cargo test --offline --workspace` all passed in this session.

This bounded completion does not cover localhost server-side file saving,
handwriting outlines, PDF ink or images, or a full browser editing journey.
Those remain separately open executable tasks.
Historical academic evidence was not independently re-audited.
